    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** serving as our undisputed anchor. With a score of 69.47, **Kyle Tucker** occupies the prime #3 spot against the manageable xERA of 4.07 presented by Landen Roupp. While our lineup faces several difficult matchups against high-end arms like the 3.01 xERA of Chase Burns, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a high-floor play at 59.35. His efficiency is buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and favorable wind conditions that help offset the talent gap against Burns. **Andy Pages** also projects well at 58.80, though we are monitoring his efficiency against the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time, which slightly caps his aggressive stolen base potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved **Heliot Ramos**, whose projection sits at a marginal 43.69. While we have him penciled into the #3 spot, his \"Lineup Pending\" status and the cold matchup against Sheehan\u2014an arm boasting a 3.16 xERA\u2014create a volatile floor. Ultimately, **Heliot Ramos** gets the nod over our remaining reserves due to the necessity of maintaining contact production, but he is the first candidate for mid-game substitution should his placement drop in the official lineup. We continue to hold **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** on the bench due to team off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our secondary depth pieces like **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Sam Antonacci** unavailable to fill gaps in today's 5x5 rotation.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the middle of our infield against Chase Burns. **Nasim Nunez** and **Brady House** both face significant downward pressure from Burns' elite 3.01 xERA, which suppresses their scoring despite the beneficial wind-out conditions at their home park. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the elite sprint speed necessary for our category scarcity strategy, we are wary of his low efficiency score (45.88). If **Drake Baldwin** (50.99) or **Liam Hicks** (52.07) fail to provide early momentum against their respective starters, we may look to pull back on aggressive base-running attempts to preserve our efficiency metrics for the remainder of the week.",
